1.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named Test, Interface-X0, action-Filter, profile-Default Profile, Enable;

2. Network \ DNS \ Settings, set DNS as 8.8.8.8(different from Neustar Server);

3. PC connects to X0, set the DNS of PC as X0 IP;

4. From PC, dig www.ea.com, do capture packet on DUT;

5. Check the DNS Packets.

2.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named Test, Interface-X0, action-Filter, profile-Default Profile, Enable;

2. Network \ DNS \ Settings, set DNS as 8.8.8.8(different from Neustar Server);

3. PC connects to X0, set the DNS of PC as X0 IP;

4. From PC, dig www.ea.com, do capture packet on DUT;

5. Check the DNS Packets.

6. Disable "Test" policy, repeat 4-5.

2.result:
In step 5, DNS Packets from PC is forwarded to Neustar server(156.154.54.200/201) by DUT;

In step 6, DNS Packets from PC is dropped by DUT.

*Delete any new policies created after this test for the next test.

3.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named Test, Interface-X0, action-Filter, Profile-Default Profile, Enable;

2. Network \ DNS \ Settings, set DNS as 8.8.8.8(different from Neustar Server);

3. PC connects to X0, set the DNS of PC as X0 IP;

4. From PC, dig www.ea.com, do capture packet on DUT;

5. Check the DNS Packets;

6. Object \ Profile Objects \ DNS Filtering, edit Default Profile, change the Allow action of Gaming to Negative Reply;

7. Repeat 3-4.

4.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named Test, Zone-LAN, action-Filter, profile-Default Profile, Enable;

2. Set interface X2 as LAN Zone, and Set DNS on DNS Settings as 8.8.8.8(different from Neustar Server);

3. PC connects to X2, set the DNS of PC as X2 IP;

4. From PC, dig www.ea.com, do capture packet on DUT;

5. Check the DNS Packets;

6. Change the Zone of "Test" policy and interface X2 to DMZ, repeat 4-5;

7. Change the Zone of "Test" policy and interface X2 to Custom public/trusted zone, repeat 4-5.

5.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named Test, Zone-WAN, action-Filter, profile-Default Profile, Enable;

2. Set interface X1 as WAN Zone, and set DNS on DNS Settings as 8.8.8.8(different from Neustar Server);

3. PC connects to X1, set the DNS of PC as X1 IP;

4. From PC, dig www.ea.com, do capture packet on DUT;

5. Check the DNS Packets.

6.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named Test, Zone-WLAN, action-Filter, profile-Default Profile, Enable;

2. Set X2 as WLAN interface with IP 172.16.31.1, and set DNS on DNS Settings as 8.8.8.8(different from Neustar Server);

3. Connect SonicPoint to X2;

4. Wireless PC connects to sonicpoit, set DNS server of PC as 172.16.31.1;

5. From PC, dig www.ea.com, do capture packet on DUT;

6. Check the DNS Packets;

7. Configure a WLAN tunnel Interface, Wireless pc connects to the interface, then repeat 5-6.

7.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top:
a policy named Test, Zone-SSLVPN, action-Filter, Enable, 
profile-Default Profile(category 'Gaming' is set as Forged IP action);

2. Set interface X1 as WAN Zone, and set DNS on DNS Settings as 8.8.8.8(different from Neustar Server);

3. Enable SSLVPN on WAN zone, config the DNS of Client profile as X0 interface ip 192.168.168.168, and Route as LAN Subnet;

4. Add a user with groups-SSLVPN Service and VPN Access-LAN subnet ;

5. Client connects to SSLVPN;

6. From Client, dig www.ea.com @192.168.168.168, do capture packet on DUT;

7. Check the DNS Packets.

8.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named Test, Zone-VPN, action-Filter, profile-Default Profile, Enable;

2. Set interface X1 as WAN Zone, and set DNS on DNS Settings as 8.8.8.8(different from Neustar Server);

3. Set up a Site to Site VPN to FW, remote network is X0 Subnet;

4. PC1 connects to FW X0, set DNS of PC1 as DUT X0 IP;

5. From PC1, dig www.ea.com, do capture packet on DUT;

6. Check the DNS Packets.

9.steps:
1. Add a LAN virtual Interface bounded to X0, VLAN tag-642, IP 192.168.10.1, and set DNS on DNS Settings as 8.8.8.8(different from Neustar Server);

2. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named Test, Interface-X0:V642, action-Filter, profile-Default Profile, Enable;

3. PC connects to X0:V642, set the DNS of PC as X0:V642 IP 192.168.10.1;

4. From PC, dig www.ea.com, do capture packet on DUT;

5. Check the DNS Packets;

10.steps:
1. Switching \ VLAN Trunking, add Vlan Trunk Port X2, and enable vlan 642;

2. Set X2:V642 as LAN interface with IP 192.168.10.1, and set DNS on DNS Settings as 8.8.8.8(different from Neustar Server);

3. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named Test, Interface-X2:V642, action-Filter, profile-Default Profile, Enable;

4. PC connects to X0:V642, set the DNS of PC as X2:V642 IP 192.168.10.1;

5. From PC, dig www.ea.com, do capture packet on DUT;

6. Check the DNS Packets;

11.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named TestF, Interface-X0, action-Filter, Enable;

2. Add top: a policy named TestP, Interface-X0, action-Proxy, Enable;

3. Network \ DNS \ Settings, set DNS as 10.190.202.200(different from Neustar Server);

4. PC connect to X0, set the DNS of PC as X0 IP, from PC, dig www.ea.com, do capture packet on DUT;

5. Check the DNS Packets;

6. Move "TestF" to the top, repeat 4-5.

12.steps:
1. Network \ Interfaces, set X0-192.168.168.168;

2. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named TestA, Interface-X0, Address-192.168.168.100, Service-UDP, action-Filter, Enable;

3. PC connect to X0, set the DNS of PC as 192.168.168.168, IP of PC as 192.168.168.100;

4. From PC, dig www.ea.com, do capture packet on DUT;

5. Check the DNS Packets;

6. Set IP of PC as 192.168.168.200;

7. Repeat 4-5.

13.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named TestS, Interface-X0, Service-UDP, action-Filter, Enable;

2. PC connect to X0, set the DNS of PC as X0 IP;

3. From PC, dig www.ea.com, do capture packet on DUT;

4. Check the DNS Packets;

5. From PC, dig www.ea.com +tcp, do capture packet on DUT;

6. Repeat 3-4.

14.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top: a policy named TestS, Interface-X0, Service-UDP, action-Filter, Schedule-10min, Enable;

2. PC connect to X0, set the DNS of PC as X0 IP;

3. From PC, dig www.ea.com, do capture packet on DUT;

4. Check the DNS Packets;

5. Wait for 10min, until the time is out of the schedule and the policy is grey;

6. From PC, dig www.ea.com, do capture packet on DUT;

7. Repeat 3-4.

15.steps:
1. Policy \ Rules and Policies \ DNS Rules, add top and enable a policy named TestC, Interface-X0, Service-UDP, action-Filter, Select 'Enable Connection Threshold for each Source IP'-2;

2. Log \ Settings \ Network \ DNS Security, enable 'DNS Policy Source IP Connection Limit Reached Drop'(id 1690), click edit, set Event Priority to Alert, Display Events in Log Monitor to 0, save;

3. PC connect to X0, set the DNS of PC as X0 IP, dig over 2 domains;

4. Check the packet monitor and system log.
